      "id": 1,
      "text": "Friendsville was founded in 1765 by John Friend Sr., making it Garrett County’s oldest settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitdeepcreek.com/friendsville/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors its first European settler, John Friend, who arrived before the American Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitdeepcreek.com/friendsville/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A historic rail trail follows an 1890s railbed to the old logging community of Kendall, once a mining hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitdeepcreek.com/friendsville/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Friendsville hosts an annual Friendsville Days Festival each August, featuring fireworks, live music, and a parade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
